    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen an owner is created (and read back), the API now returns a `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `displayName` field (serialized into `GET /api/owners/{id}` responses).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that computes the value via expression:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nThis follows the existing Spring/MapStruct/OpenAPI-codegen conventions in the repo (the DTO is generated from the spec; the mapper derives the field). Test result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, including `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName` which asserts `$.displayName` equals `LastName, John`.",
